            {
                "entry_id": "366bdec9-9859-3e32-95cd-2eb99962897b",
                "word": "edele",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a987dc8f-823d-483e-9ef4-12e872de0434",
                        "entry_id": "366bdec9-9859-3e32-95cd-2eb99962897b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "edelen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c454ca21-1dea-3413-8047-25f82167ac34",
                        "entry_id": "366bdec9-9859-3e32-95cd-2eb99962897b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand van adel, een adellijk persoon"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2acf088-e910-42ff-8bff-ad3dbe2fee2f",
                                "sense_id": "c454ca21-1dea-3413-8047-25f82167ac34",
                                "text": "De edele zorgde dat het landgoed goed werd bestuurd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68f09896-3125-4e4c-aeda-02f0d376075c",
                                "sense_id": "c454ca21-1dea-3413-8047-25f82167ac34",
                                "text": "Als een slordige s in spiegelbeeld was het kanaal over de stadsplattegrond gekalkt door een dronken ontwerper die sadistisch lachte toen hij zag hoe zijn ingreep de stad zo goed als onbegaanbaar had gemaakt voor de flanerende edelen met hun satijnen schoentjes en die pas de volgende dag, weer nuchter, besefte dat hij geheel tegen zijn bedoeling in een magnifieke waterweg had geschapen die alle delen van de stad op een mooie, trage manier met elkaar verbond."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e90cce03-ec11-4373-856d-ead143aefb9d",
                        "source_entry_id": "366bdec9-9859-3e32-95cd-2eb99962897b",
                        "source_sense_id": "c454ca21-1dea-3413-8047-25f82167ac34",
                        "source_sense_description": "iemand van adel",
                        "target_lang_word": "noble",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "noble",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c1b9266-b562-3e2b-a5d5-c7f614557a14",
                                        "entry_id": "3a5b3128-4a12-32ba-b300-d3a7e06d8194",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An aristocrat; one of aristocratic blood."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f85b268c-8a0a-4b56-b99d-7eb32cab631a",
                                                "sense_id": "0c1b9266-b562-3e2b-a5d5-c7f614557a14",
                                                "text": "This country house was occupied by nobles in the 16th century."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c454d846-9706-3955-8c18-97992a248902",
                                        "entry_id": "3a5b3128-4a12-32ba-b300-d3a7e06d8194",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A medieval gold coin of England in the 14th and 15th centuries, usually valued at 6s 8d."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bdc04fb4-3b82-46bc-8f2e-92a8b45b34e8",
                                                "sense_id": "c454d846-9706-3955-8c18-97992a248902",
                                                "text": "I lyked no thynge his playe, / For yf I had not quyckely fledde the touche, / He had plucte oute the nobles of my pouche."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b427eaf4-d199-4631-968d-de8a3f37f29a",
                                                "sense_id": "c454d846-9706-3955-8c18-97992a248902",
                                                "text": "And who shall then stick closest to ye, and excite others? not he who takes up armes for cote and conduct, and his four nobles of Danegelt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f80cb79-fe7e-47cf-8b49-331d8f0872bf",
                                                "sense_id": "c454d846-9706-3955-8c18-97992a248902",
                                                "text": "There, before the high altar, as the choir's voices soared upwards to the blue, star-flecked ceiling, Henry knelt and made his offering of a ‘noble in gold’, 6s 8d."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "noble",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa0dadbe-1cac-3968-816d-db57cf7585d3",
                                        "entry_id": "3e970cf1-dba5-3fa6-b97d-e16d84927814",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having honorable qualities; having moral eminence and freedom from anything petty, mean or dubious in conduct and character."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5eee5f6a-c115-4a89-8b78-d27345169561",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0dadbe-1cac-3968-816d-db57cf7585d3",
                                                "text": "He made a noble effort."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0091c5ad-5014-416d-bee5-82657dbcbcfb",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0dadbe-1cac-3968-816d-db57cf7585d3",
                                                "text": "He is a noble man who would never put his family in jeopardy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cad53633-19e3-426d-8d19-928f46a89a8e",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0dadbe-1cac-3968-816d-db57cf7585d3",
                                                "text": "Korben, I realize you must be pretty mad at me. But I want you to know that I am fighting for a noble cause. / Yes, you're trying to save the world. I remember."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "677dd678-19da-3496-bf83-f63b01fc872d",
                                        "entry_id": "3e970cf1-dba5-3fa6-b97d-e16d84927814",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Grand; stately; magnificent; splendid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ed85ae4-cb53-4d0f-a604-02979c24f8b5",
                                                "sense_id": "677dd678-19da-3496-bf83-f63b01fc872d",
                                                "text": "a noble edifice"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e05feb94-3540-4707-a93e-4a3610e83154",
                                                "sense_id": "677dd678-19da-3496-bf83-f63b01fc872d",
                                                "text": "He was thinking; but the glory of the song, the swell from the great organ, the clustered lights, […], the height and vastness of this noble fane, its antiquity and its strength—all these things seemed to have their part as causes of the thrilling emotion that accompanied his thoughts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1dd52a6c-d603-3b14-8e8e-6dbf8cc0fe8a",
                                        "entry_id": "3e970cf1-dba5-3fa6-b97d-e16d84927814",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of exalted rank; of or relating to the nobility; distinguished from the masses by birth, station, or title; highborn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ec75f24-f966-49a0-9dd4-efac17e433a3",
                                                "sense_id": "1dd52a6c-d603-3b14-8e8e-6dbf8cc0fe8a",
                                                "text": "noble blood; a noble personage"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
